        "at": "2026-10-26T15:55:56"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "BLUF",
      "narration_text": "The short version. You do not send text to a voice model. The text is converted to sounds first, and the model never sees your words. And the voice itself is not a recording of anyone. It is a small block of numbers.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type-on",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "BrutalistHesitantWriter",
          "props": {
            "face": "serif",
            "align": "center",
            "fontSize": 200,
            "lineSpacing": 1.16,
            "charMs": 18,
            "hesitateBetween": 0,
            "hesitateWithin": 0,
            "mistakeRate": 0,
            "jitter": 5,
            "text": "Not text.\nSounds.\nAnd the voice\nis just a file."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-26T19:24:19.467383+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 18,
      "actual_duration_s": 11.9,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 11.916666666666666,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:BrutalistHesitantWriter",
        "at": "2026-10-26T15:55:56"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "WHAT",
      "narration_text": "Every call runs the same three steps. Your text is turned into phonemes, which are the units of sound. The model turns those phonemes into raw audio samples. And the samples get written to a file. That is the whole pipeline.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeTldrWhat",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "VOICE",
            "heading": "Three steps, every time",
            "greeting": "",
            "topic": "",
            "question": "So what is a call to a voice model?",
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "lines": [
              "Your text becomes phonemes",
              "The model turns those into samples",
              "The samples become a file"
            ]
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-26T19:25:24.801985+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 19,
      "actual_duration_s": 12.54,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 12.541666666666666,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeTldrWhat",
        "at": "2026-10-26T15:55:56"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "TERMS",
      "narration_text": "Four terms worth having. A phoneme is one unit of speech sound. A voice here is a block of numbers rather than a recording of a person. The sample rate is how many points of audio are stored for every second. And inference is just running the model from input to output.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeDefinitions",
          "props": {
            "title": "Four terms",
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "terms": [
              {
                "term": "Phoneme",
                "meaning": "One unit of speech sound"
              },
              {
                "term": "Voice",
                "meaning": "A block of numbers, not a recording"
              },
              {
                "term": "Sample rate",
                "meaning": "Audio points stored per second"
              },
              {
                "term": "Inference",
                "meaning": "Running the model, start to finish"
              }
            ]
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-26T19:26:04.701244+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 22,
      "actual_duration_s": 14.98,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 15.0,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeDefinitions",
        "at": "2026-10-26T15:55:56"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "EVIDENCE",
      "narration_text": "Here is that first step on my own machine. I gave it the phrase calling voice A I. What came back is the same phrase written in the international phonetic alphabet, with the stress marks included. That string is what the model actually receives.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeCodeBeat",
          "props": {
            "title": "phonemes.txt",
            "language": "text",
            "largeText": true,
            "brandLabel": "Irreducibly Human",
            "sparkLine": "The model never sees your words.",
            "code": "in  = \"Calling voice AI.\"\nout = kˈɔːlɪŋ vˈɔɪs\n      ˌeɪˈaɪ."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B04.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-26T19:26:32.909894+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 21,
      "actual_duration_s": 13.16,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 13.166666666666666,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeCodeBeat",
        "at": "2026-10-26T15:55:56"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "EVIDENCE",
      "narration_text": "And here is the call itself. One function, with the text and the name of a voice. What comes back is an array of numbers and a sample rate. Twenty four thousand points per second, stored as thirty two bit floats. No audio file yet. Just numbers.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeCodeBeat",
          "props": {
            "title": "synth.py",
            "language": "python",
            "largeText": true,
            "brandLabel": "Irreducibly Human",
            "sparkLine": "One line in. Numbers out.",
            "code": "samples, sr = k.create(\n    text,\n    voice=\"am_onyx\")\n# sr = 24000\n# dtype = float32"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B05.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-26T19:27:02.036416+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 21,
      "actual_duration_s": 13.44,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 13.458333333333334,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeCodeBeat",
        "at": "2026-10-26T15:55:56"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "act": "EVIDENCE",
      "narration_text": "This is what the whole thing weighs. The model is three hundred and ten megabytes. Every voice it can do lives in a second file of twenty six megabytes. Fifty four voices in total, across nine languages. It ran on my laptop, with no account and no key, and it cost nothing.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "build-on",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeVerdictArtifact",
          "props": {
